      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <array>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass FrequencyTable {\n  static constexpr uint32_t table_size = 2048;\n  static constexpr uint32_t table_mask = table_size - 1;\n  static constexpr uint16_t count_bits = 10;\n  static constexpr uint16_t count_mask = (uint16_t{1} << count_bits) - 1;\n  static constexpr uint16_t generation_limit = uint16_t{1} << (16 - count_bits);\n\n  array<int, table_size> keys_;\n  array<uint16_t, table_size> entries_{};\n  uint16_t generation_ = 1;\n\n  static uint32_t slot_for(int key) {\n    uint32_t value = static_cast<uint32_t>(key);\n    value ^= value >> 16;\n    value *= 0x7feb352dU;\n    value ^= value >> 15;\n    value *= 0x846ca68bU;\n    value ^= value >> 16;\n    return value & table_mask;\n  }\n\n public:\n  void clear() {\n    ++generation_;\n    if (generation_ == generation_limit) {\n      entries_.fill(0);\n      generation_ = 1;\n    }\n  }\n\n  int get(int key) const {\n    uint32_t slot = slot_for(key);\n    uint16_t entry = entries_[slot];\n    while ((entry >> count_bits) == generation_) {\n      if (keys_[slot] == key) return entry & count_mask;\n      slot = (slot + 1) & table_mask;\n      entry = entries_[slot];\n    }\n    return 0;\n  }\n\n  void add(int key) {\n    uint32_t slot = slot_for(key);\n    uint16_t entry = entries_[slot];\n    while ((entry >> count_bits) == generation_) {\n      if (keys_[slot] == key) {\n        entries_[slot] = static_cast<uint16_t>(entry + 1);\n        return;\n      }\n      slot = (slot + 1) & table_mask;\n      entry = entries_[slot];\n    }\n    keys_[slot] = key;\n    entries_[slot] = static_cast<uint16_t>((generation_ << count_bits) | 1);\n  }\n};\n\nlong long solve(const vector<int>& matrix, int bound_count, int scan_count, int k) {\n  const int* const values = matrix.data();\n  long long answer = 0;\n\n#pragma omp parallel reduction(+ : answer)\n  {\n    vector<int> row_sums(scan_count);\n    FrequencyTable frequency;\n    long long subtotal = 0;\n\n#pragma omp for schedule(dynamic, 1) nowait\n    for (int first = 0; first < bound_count; ++first) {\n      fill(row_sums.begin(), row_sums.end(), 0);\n\n      for (int last = first; last < bound_count; ++last) {\n        const int* const next_band = values + static_cast<size_t>(last) * scan_count;\n\n#pragma omp simd\n        for (int index = 0; index < scan_count; ++index) {\n          row_sums[index] += next_band[index];\n        }\n\n        frequency.clear();\n        frequency.add(0);\n        int prefix = 0;\n        for (int index = 0; index < scan_count; ++index) {\n          prefix += row_sums[index];\n          subtotal += frequency.get(prefix - k);\n          frequency.add(prefix);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n\n    answer += subtotal;\n  }\n\n  return answer;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n  cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n\n  vector<int> matrix(static_cast<size_t>(m) * n);\n  int bound_count;\n  int scan_count;\n\n  if (m <= n) {\n    bound_count = m;\n    scan_count = n;\n    for (int row = 0; row < m; ++row) {\n      for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n        cin >> matrix[static_cast<size_t>(row) * scan_count + column];\n      }\n    }\n  } else {\n    bound_count = n;\n    scan_count = m;\n    for (int row = 0; row < m; ++row) {\n      for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n        cin >> matrix[static_cast<size_t>(column) * scan_count + row];\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  cout << solve(matrix, bound_count, scan_count, k) << '\\n';\n  return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/main.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Packing each frequency-table slot's generation tag and bounded count into one 16-bit entry reduces the cache footprint and memory loads in the sequential prefix-frequency loop, while retaining SIMD only for the independent contiguous strip update.",
  "notes": "The ordered prefix loop is deliberately not SIMD-annotated because each prefix and frequency update depends on its predecessor. A 10-bit count safely holds at most scan_count + 1 <= 1000 occurrences; the remaining six bits provide lazy clearing with a full reset before tag reuse.",
